    "teacher_markdown": "**Tell AI exactly what you want to see**\r\n- Have students read over their prompt to \"see\" their web app in their mind. \r\n- If their requirements are too vague for them to visualize the webpage, encourage them to add at least one specific detail. The more detailed and specific their prompt, the more likely AI is to build exactly what they are envisioning. \r\n\r\n**Emphasize iteration, not perfection.**  \r\n- The goal is not to “win” the best design — it’s to practice prompting AI and refining work.\r\n- Check that students save AI generated code with clear, short comments (e.g., “Added hero section”)\r\n\r\n**Big Idea Reminder:**  \r\n  - AI is a collaborator, not an autopilot.\r\n  - Prompt clarity matters.",
    "display_name": "The Green Gardener",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Sam needs a digital plant-tracking app and watering schedule.",
